  "headline": "Two main lifts dropped this week — Barbell Bench Press and Barbell Back Squat are both down, signalling it's time to back off.",
  "items": [
    {
      "rule": "deload",
      "action": "Take one lighter week with the same exercises. Run Barbell Bench Press, Barbell Row, Barbell Back Squat, Romanian Deadlift, and Overhead Press at roughly half their current sets (so about 4 sets each instead of 8) and use clearly lighter weights than this week's bests — think 60–65% of your normal loads rather than pushing close to them. Keep total sessions at whatever feels easy, not 6. After the lighter week, build back up gradually from there."
